    - sketch  # bef8
    isbefore: []  # bef8
    duplicate_of: []  # bef8
    not_duplicate_of: []  # bef8
    pr_ref:  # bef8
    description: "Source: a second outside reader (a fresh LLM session given only the help output and the cached files) reviewed a hypergumbo 9.2.0 self-run on 2026-11-13, cache f36c63310c791188/results/c872eb7a7e793eab/ac34c56c06ec1788, made after the fixes from the first review merged. Each claim was re-checked against those files and the code on dev fed15705d7, then measured on 20 repositories that are not hypergumbo (default sketch and --no-source, 8k/32k/128k). Scripts, the 120 sketches and results.txt: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/outside_reader_review2_11142026.\n\nOBSERVED on the self-run, sketch Configuration section, \"--- Additional context (semantic) ---\" block: the quoted lines carry no file name (four pairs of \"  > ...\" lines with nothing saying which of nine pyproject.toml files each is from), and the block ends with seven blank lines inside the code fence.\n\nMECHANISM. _extract_config_embedding returns, per file, a heading line \"[path]\", its quoted lines and an empty separator line. The merge in the hybrid extractor then drops any line that shares more than two words longer than three characters with the heuristic lines above it. The test is applied to each line on its own. A heading \"[packages/hypergumbo-core/pyproject.toml]\" repeats words the heuristic lines already hold (the package name, pyproject.toml), so headings are dropped; their quotes and separators are kept. Reproduced by calling the function on this repository: 8 of 10 headings dropped, every separator kept. When a file's quotes are all dropped too, its separator remains alone. Not traced: which later step leaves exactly seven separators at the end.\n\nASK. Apply the redundancy test to a file's block as a unit: a heading stays if any of its quotes stays, and goes with its separator if none does. No output line of the section is blank except one between blocks. Related open items on the same block: INV-kukaf-ruti (the --config-extraction flag is ignored when the survey precomputes config_info) and WI-samif-gosuf (previews cut mid-token).\n\nGENERALITY (owner, 2026-11-13). The fix must be a rule that holds for any repository and any language. The hypergumbo self-run is only where the defect was first seen. A fix keyed to this repository's paths or file names, or one that works for one language only, does not close this item.\nThe rule is on the shape of the block (heading, quotes, separator), not on any file name; it holds for every manifest type the semantic extractor reads. Not measured on other repositories: the analysis script's check for trailing blank lines found none on the 20, and it did not check for missing headings."  # bef8
    fields: {}  # bef8
