- op: discuss  # ebcb
  at: '2026-11-14T09:47:51Z'  # ebcb
  by: agent  # ebcb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ebcb
  clock: 3  # ebcb
  nonce: ebcb  # ebcb
  message: "Fixed in PR #2183, in two commits because the cure first went into one of two passes. (1) sketch._new_semantic_blocks applies the redundancy test to quoted lines only and keeps or drops a file's block as a unit, so a heading stays exactly when one of its quotes does. (2) The lines are regrouped by file once more before printing (_extract_config_info); that pass added its own separator after blocks that still carried theirs, and took only a name with a dot for a heading, so [Dockerfile] and [Makefile] were folded into the file above. MEASURED on the 20 repositories: quotes with no heading were on the self-run only (0 of the 17 other sketches that have the block); a doubled blank line was in 8 of 17 before, and still in the same 8 after commit (1) alone, which is how pass (2) was found. After commit (2), _extract_config_info in hybrid mode on alertmanager, knex and pm2 (three of the 8) returns no doubled blank line and 10, 4 and 3 headings; the 20-repository run was not repeated after commit (2). Tests: test_sketch_config_semantic_blocks.py, through _extract_config_info in hybrid mode."  # ebcb
